WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.260
I got to tell you,

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:03.080
this is an interesting time we are in.

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.500
And I think you're
responding the same way I am,

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.160
which is just letting my hair grow.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:08.580
Your hair has gotten quite long.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.626
It really has. Yes.

00:00:10.626 --> 00:00:14.660
It's been seven months or so
since I've had a hair cut.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.460
It's very much off-brand for me.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.380
I know, you're you're
always the clean cut look.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:22.050
I find myself doing this a lot now.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.003
I'm doing a lot of stuff with my fingers

00:00:25.003 --> 00:00:26.330
to move my hair around,

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:29.370
like I'm sort of like a
Charlie's angels you know.

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:32.450
I've been amusing my children with this.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:33.400
Let's see it.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.453
I do that.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.598
Pretty good.

00:00:36.598 --> 00:00:39.306
And then I tell them
about flock of seagulls,

00:00:39.306 --> 00:00:41.878
(both laugh)

00:00:41.878 --> 00:00:42.970
and they leave the room.

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:44.740
Yeah, no one really
wants to hear about that.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.330
You know we found this picture of you.

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:48.698
I think this is you in high school.

00:00:48.698 --> 00:00:50.740
(Andy laughs)

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.643
What's the story with this photo?

00:00:54.358 --> 00:00:56.100
You looked like you had no idea

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.520
that your picture was being taken.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:58.730
What's going on?

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:00.760
Well, that was junior year of high school.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.740
I took that picture for the yearbook,

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:05.150
but they gave me a chance to retake it,

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:06.100
and I took them up on that.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.210
So that's actually a
rejected yearbook photo

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:09.050
that no one's ever seen before.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:10.910
You're kidding. This was rejected?

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:12.330
I rejected that one.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.600
But look, my hair is
getting back there now.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:15.660
Yeah, you're getting back there.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:16.770
Oh, look guess what.

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:19.090
You can tell now this was
an innocent young man.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:20.750
And when I look at this guy,

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.060
the new Andy Daley,

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:23.670
the current day Andy Daly,

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:25.700
I see a man who's lost his soul.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.530
Yes, clearly.

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:29.350
But I want to see if I can get that smile,

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:30.620
if I can duplicate that smile.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:31.770
Cause I don't know what that smile

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:33.520
was trying to communicate.
What does that smile say?

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:34.400
Can you get it back?

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.233
It's like, "What's up future?"

00:01:36.233 --> 00:01:37.066
(man laughs)

00:01:37.066 --> 00:01:37.899
"Hey, future,

00:01:37.899 --> 00:01:40.966
I'm ready for whatever you got."

00:01:40.966 --> 00:01:42.280
(Andy laughs)

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.960
Can I show you one of the weirdest parts,

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.630
I still have that I still have that tie.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:48.428
Why do I still have that time?

00:01:48.428 --> 00:01:51.533
No. That's sad that you have that tie.

00:01:51.533 --> 00:01:52.930
It's what? It's sad.
I mean,

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:54.540
Not sad, impressive.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.010
(Andy laughs)

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.050
It's one or the other.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.950
I don't know which one it is.
60/40

